i got the new official xbox wireless  headset right here and i'm doing this  review to let you know whether or not  it's worth the 100  price tag and to give you a little hint  it's really good  xbox has been kind of leaning into the  sleek minimalist look with its hardware  while packing in some high-end specs and  that design philosophy  extends to the new wireless headset it  has impressive build quality high sound  quality some important features like  simultaneous bluetooth connectivity  dolby atmos and it was really  comfortable in my experience though that  does come with some conditions that  we'll get into later  but overall for 100 bucks this is  probably one of your best  options if xbox is your preferred  platform  there's so much more to get into though  so let's get into it  let's start by talking about the overall  build quality you get a sense of that as  soon as you take it out of the box and  hold it and you can see that it's very  flexible when you start to stretch  and contort it at least within reason  there's no audible creaking and it  certainly doesn't feel like it's going  to be cracking  it also helps that there isn't any fancy  design work on this headset it's just  plain black plastic subtle neon green  trim and the xbox logo on the right ear  cup  it's straightforward without many moving  parts or over-the-top branding  in terms of comfort the pseudo leather  and foam ear pads provided some  top-notch cushioning  for long sessions but as it is with any  leather-like  upholstery it will get sweaty after a  few hours but one thing to note is that  the headset  does clamp pretty tightly thankfully for  me  the pads provided more than enough  cushioning to kind of alleviate that  pressure but if you do have a bigger  head  then i do i like to think i have a  fairly normal sized head that is one  thing that you will  have to take into consideration another  thing that you should know is that for  these to fit properly on me  i had to extend the headband to its  maximum length  as you can see here you can adjust each  ear cup as you would do it any other  headset  and i have them extended to their max  length here and that's how i get them to  fit properly on me  so if you have a bigger head or if you  have very voluminous hair  you might have some issues getting these  on to fit properly  now let's talk about features it has  most of the essentials you'd want out of  a mid to high-end audio device  as with any wireless xbox designed  accessory this headset uses microsoft's  proprietary wireless tech that lets you  sync directly to a console without a  dongle or cable  just hold down the power button on the  headset and press the pairing button on  the xbox  and you're good this thing also rocks  bluetooth 4.2 and you can simultaneously  pair it to another device  in addition to your console for example  i was on discord  chatting and listening to a group of  friends through my phone  while gaming on my xbox series x the  leading audio technologies are also  available when using the xbox wireless  headset  both dolby atmos and dts headphone x can  be enabled in the console  settings although you do need separate  access to the respective applications  to utilize those features alternatively  you have windows sonic available for  free  which provides an improved audio  experience for the headset  now for features on the headset you have  volume control  relegated to the right ear cup it works  as a dial so if you want to  crank up the volume you just go like  that  and if you want to turn down the volume  you go like that  it's a pretty clever design i like it a  lot and if you want to adjust chat and  audio mix  it's on the left ear cup so there's kind  of a tactile feedback you get when it's  at  balanced perfectly at 50 50 but if you  want to turn in the turn up the in-game  volume a little bit more over chat you  just twist it like that and if you want  to hear chat a little bit more  you twist it the other way like that  it's pretty neat  another design choice that i like is the  microphone so it folds  in like that and then it extends outward  like that with a flexible rubber casing  that stays in place  and when you're using it it doesn't  extend that far  so it's not it's not in front of your  mouth so if you're eating or drinking  it doesn't get in the way as for battery  life i was impressed with how  it was able to hold up after a full  charge microsoft states that a 30 minute  charge should provide around four hours  of use and a three hour charge will  allow the headset to last about 15 hours  i charged it overnight and after using  it for about eight hours in a day  the xbox ui indicated that the battery  remained well above half  full now let's get into the most  important aspect of a headset  sound quality now i wouldn't claim to be  an audio file but good audio is very  important for the games that i play  having the proper sound stage and having  high quality music for some of the best  soundtracks that i love in games  so what i do is i run a sennheiser hd598  and i run it through a dac on my pc now  the xbox wireless headset  isn't necessarily going to stack up  against a 300 dollar setup  but if you are coming off of earbuds  that you're plugging into your  controller  or if you're using tv speakers or a  budget level headset  you are going to notice a significant  difference when jumping to the xbox  wireless headset  you'll hear a solid bass coming through  on default settings which is great for  games with bombastic moments  and impactful audio design music will  also sound bolder  and without the bass drowning out the  other frequencies even as you kick up  the volume there isn't much distortion  that comes through in the mids and highs  so the audio isn't abrasive  if you want it to get louder now at near  max volume you may notice that the audio  details get lost or muddled  and the highs can be a bit harsh but at  that point you should probably be  turning down the volume a bit  now i tested sound quality with games  like forza horizon 4  doom eternal and tetris effect connected  all of which feature emphatic audio  design  but in different styles overall  everything sounded great and had me  excited to turn up the volume on my  favorite games and tunes  now positional audio is very distinct so  competitive gamers should be satisfied  with the advantage they can get out of  the xbox wireless headset  audio cues were easy to pick up when  playing gears 5 multiplayer which  allowed me to better anticipate enemies  approaching from specific locations  directional sound makes the audio  experience in non-competitive games feel  more full as well  while playing ori and the will of the  wisps for example i noticed the  direction of ori's attacks  left and right was represented sonically  which was subtle  but effective it's also nice when the  whimsical soundtrack comes through with  great clarity at the same time  i had a similar experience in an older  game like lost odyssey  where the high quality audio gave a new  edge to the cutscenes and made nobuo  uematsu's incredible compositions shine  brighter  as for the microphone quality it's  functional your voice will come through  well enough for others to hear you  clearly but it's nothing to get excited  about if crystal clear communication is  key for you  you might want to look elsewhere for  example here's my voice using the  microphone on the xbox wireless headset  testing testing 123 xbox wireless  headset  microphone quality test so overall  i really like this headset it has high  quality sound it's super durable  and i just like the sleek minimalist  look of this thing and it was very  comfortable in my experience though that  is something that you're going to want  to look into a little bit more for  yourself  but to put it in simple terms if you're  willing to drop a hundred dollars on a  headset for your xbox  you can't go wrong with the new xbox  wireless headset now if you want more  details on my experience  head on over to gamespot.com and check  out the full written review  which is also linked in the description  box below thank you for watching  and we'll see you next time  [Music]  [Music]  you
 

